  "term": "temperament trait",
  "definition": "In mental health, a temperament trait is a biologically based emotional component of personality in Cloninger’s model. The packet describes temperamental traits as moderately heritable, present early in life, and relatively stable across the lifespan, in contrast to character, which develops through social learning and maturation.",
